{"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This article covers the most common errors and unexpected behaviors you may encounter, along with their causes and solutions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Route Not Found","type":"heading","anchor":"Route-Not-Found"},{"level":3,"text":"Symptom","type":"heading","anchor":"Symptom"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A route is pushed but no view appears, or an error message is displayed:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["Route 'DetailRoute' are not define in 'HomeRoute'"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Cause","type":"heading","anchor":"Cause"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftRouting renders an error view when the resolved route cannot be cast to the expected "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteDestination","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" type. This typically happens when a route from one enum is pushed into a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingView","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" configured for a different destination."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Solution","type":"heading","anchor":"Solution"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Ensure the pushed route matches the destination type of the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" it targets:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ ✅ Correct — route and destination match","router.push(HomeRoute.detail(id: 42))","","\/\/ ❌ Wrong — route type doesn't match the active RoutingView","router.push(SettingsRoute.profile)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"ErrorView Behavior","type":"heading","anchor":"ErrorView-Behavior"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When a route cannot be resolved, an error view is rendered. Its behavior depends on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Configuration.shouldCrashOnRouteNotFound"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"shouldCrashOnRouteNotFound","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Behavior"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"text":" (default)","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Displays the error message inline as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Text","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Crashes the app with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fatalError"}]}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"code":"true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" during development to catch routing mismatches immediately. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ConfigurationGuide","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" for setup details."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"onAppear Fires Before the Root When Pushing Into an Unvisited Tab","type":"heading","anchor":"onAppear-Fires-Before-the-Root-When-Pushing-Into-an-Unvisited-Tab"},{"level":3,"text":"Symptom","type":"heading","anchor":"Symptom"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tabRouter.push(_:in:)"},{"text":" (and similarly ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"present"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cover"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"popToRoot"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"update(root:in:)"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handle(tabDeeplink:)"},{"text":") switches to the target tab and acts on it in the same call. If that tab’s stack was never shown before, the pushed route’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"text":" can fire ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the tab’s root ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"text":" – the opposite of what a real, incremental push does.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Cause","type":"heading","anchor":"Cause"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tab change and the push both happen synchronously, before SwiftUI re-renders. If the target tab was never selected before, its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NavigationStack(path:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is being shown for the very first time – with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"path"},{"type":"text","text":" already non-empty. SwiftUI never gets a frame where that stack shows just the root; it materializes the whole stack (root + pushed route) at once instead of running a normal push transition, and doesn’t guarantee "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onAppear"},{"type":"text","text":" fires root-first in that situation."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is a SwiftUI rendering-order quirk, not a SwiftRouting bug – there’s no fix on our side to guarantee ordering here. It isn’t specific to ","type":"text"},{"code":"push(_:in:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" either: the same applies to any router method that changes tab and acts in the same call, and to deep links that land on a not-yet-visited tab.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Solution","type":"heading","anchor":"Solution"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Don’t rely on ","type":"text"},{"code":"onAppear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"onDisappear","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ordering after a cross-tab push\/present\/deeplink into a tab that hasn’t been shown yet. If you need reliable ordering (for logging, analytics, etc.), key off ","type":"text"},{"code":"Configuration.logger","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"Configuration.events","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instead (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ConfigurationGuide"},{"text":") – ","type":"text"},{"code":".action(.changeTab(_:))","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":".navigation(...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" are logged synchronously, in the correct causal order, at the moment the router methods are called, regardless of when SwiftUI actually renders each view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Context Not Received","type":"heading","anchor":"Context-Not-Received"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If a context is sent but no observer is triggered, check:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The observer is registered ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the context is sent.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The observer is registered on the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"parent","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" router, not the child."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The context type matches exactly on both the sender and the observer side.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["\/\/ Parent — register before navigation","router.add(context: UserSelectionContext.self) { [weak self] context in","    self?.selectedUser = context.selectedUser","}","","\/\/ Child — send context","router.context(UserSelectionContext(selectedUser: user))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Memory Leaks with Contexts","type":"heading","anchor":"Memory-Leaks-with-Contexts"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Retain cycles occur when closures capture ","type":"text"},{"code":"self","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" strongly. Always use ","type":"text"},{"code":"[weak self]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when referencing class instances:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ ❌ Retain cycle","router.add(context: MyContext.self) { context in","    self.handle(context)","}","","\/\/ ✅ Correct","router.add(context: MyContext.self) { [weak self] context in","    self?.handle(context)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Observers registered outside of a view lifecycle (e.g., in a ViewModel) must be removed explicitly. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContextGuide","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for the full memory management guide."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Visualizing the Router Hierarchy","type":"heading","anchor":"Visualizing-the-Router-Hierarchy"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When it’s unclear which router owns which tab\/sheet\/cover, what the full navigation stack looks like, or which "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RouteContext"},{"type":"text","text":" observers are registered on which router, print the whole hierarchy to the console. Both variants are only available in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DEBUG"},{"type":"text","text":" builds – calls are compiled out entirely in release, so there’s no need to remove them before shipping."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"printRouter(trigger:)"},{"type":"text","text":" to print the tree on appear and again whenever a value changes, for example the current route:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["content.printRouter(trigger: router.currentRoute)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This prints the tree starting from the top-most router, for example. Every stack-based router gets a ","type":"text"},{"code":"root:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" line, and a ","type":"text"},{"code":"path:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" line for anything pushed on top of it (omitted when nothing has been pushed) – so you’re not just seeing the current route in isolation. A split router also gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"content:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"detail:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lines for its column selections, since ","type":"text"},{"code":"current:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alone only shows whichever one currently “wins” (an explicit push, then detail, then content):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["router(app) — current: home","   root: home","├─ tabRouter(hometab) — current: home","│  ├─ router(tab(home)) — current: profile(userId: \"42\")","│  │     root: home","│  │     path: [profile(userId: \"42\")]","│  │     contexts: [UserSelectionContext(profile(userId: \"42\"))]","│  └─ router(tab(settings)) — current: settings","│        root: settings","├─ router(split(sidebar)) — current: player(id: \"42\")","│     root: sidebar","│     content: players(type: .forward)","│     detail: player(id: \"42\")","└─ router(presented(sheet)) — current: onboarding","      root: onboarding"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"printRouterOnChange()"},{"text":" to re-print whenever a router in the hierarchy logs a meaningful event (push, present, tab change, router creation\/destruction…), without picking a specific value to watch — including at the very top of the app, before any child router exists yet. This is the noisier of the two variants; routine or redundant events (view appearance, going back, context execution…) are filtered out to keep it from firing multiple times for the same conceptual change:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["content.printRouterOnChange()"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"Placement relative to `.environment(\\.router, ...)`","type":"heading","anchor":"Placement-relative-to-environmentrouter-"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Like any modifier reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Environment(\\.router)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"printRouter*()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only sees the router injected by an ","type":"text"},{"code":".environment(\\.router, ...)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call that comes ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"after","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" it in the modifier chain (i.e. applied further out). If ","type":"text"},{"code":".environment()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" comes first, the modifier is outside its reach and silently falls back to the disconnected default router — it never crashes, it just never prints anything meaningful:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ ❌ Wrong — .environment() is \"inside\" printRouterOnChange(); the modifier","\/\/ never sees the real router and instead observes the inert default one.","ChoiceScreen()","    .environment(\\.router, Router(configuration: .default))","    .printRouterOnChange()","","\/\/ ✅ Correct — .environment() is the outermost modifier, so it covers","\/\/ printRouterOnChange() too.","ChoiceScreen()","    .printRouterOnChange()","    .environment(\\.router, Router(configuration: .default))"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"title":"Troubleshooting","roleHeading":"API Collection","modules":[{"name":"SwiftRouting"}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Troubleshooting"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting"]]},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Diagnose and fix common issues encountered when using SwiftRouting."}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"title":"Related","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ConfigurationGuide","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContextGuide","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Configuration","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContext","doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouterModel"],"anchor":"Related"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Support","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/FAQ"],"anchor":"Support","generated":true}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/troubleshooting"]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/RouteDestination":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routedestination","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RouteDestination"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"RouteDestination","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteDestination","abstract":[{"text":"Protocol that associates a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Route","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with its corresponding ","type":"text"},{"code":"View","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RouteDestination"}]},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/RouteContext":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContext","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A type that can be used to pass data between routes and trigger navigation flow completions.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","title":"RouteContext","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"typealias"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RouteContext"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routecontext","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RouteContext"}]},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/RoutingView":{"kind":"symbol","title":"RoutingView","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RoutingView","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routingview","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RoutingView","abstract":[{"text":"Creates a navigation container with its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"Router","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RoutingView","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/Configuration":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/Configuration","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Configuration","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/configuration","title":"Configuration","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Configuration","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A configuration structure used to initialize the app router."}]},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/FAQ":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/faq","title":"FAQ","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/FAQ","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Answers to common questions about SwiftRouting usage and design decisions."}],"role":"collectionGroup","kind":"article"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/RouteContextGuide":{"type":"topic","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouteContextGuide","abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to pass data between routes using RouteContext.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routecontextguide","kind":"article","title":"Route Context"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting":{"title":"SwiftRouting","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A lightweight, type-safe navigation framework built on top of NavigationStack for SwiftUI."}]},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/RouterModel":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/routermodel","abstract":[{"text":"Defines navigation capabilities within a ","type":"text"},{"code":"ViewModel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or other components.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"RouterModel","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"RouterModel","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/RouterModel","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RouterModel","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftRouting/documentation/SwiftRouting/ConfigurationGuide":{"kind":"article","role":"collectionGroup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to configure SwiftRouting and customize logging behavior."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftrouting\/configurationguide","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftRouting\/documentation\/SwiftRouting\/ConfigurationGuide","type":"topic","title":"Configuration and Logging"}}}